From: OpenWrt WR11000 port
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: skip RSSI chain stats for vdevs the host does not track

On the Cudy WR11000 (IPQ5332 + dual-MAC QCN9224) an MLO station that
reconnected across three links made every station statistics call
fail. The per-chain RSSI request is sent with vdev_id 0, and the
firmware answers with entries for the STA vdevs it has on that pdev.
One of them could not be matched to a host link vif:

  ath12k_wifi7_pci 0001:01:00.0: No VIF found for vdev 1
  ath12k_wifi7_pci 0001:01:00.0: not found vif for vdev id 1
  ath12k_wifi7_pci 0001:01:00.0: failed to pull fw stats: -71
  ath12k_wifi7_pci 0001:01:00.0: time out while waiting for get fw stats

about once a second from then on. ath12k_wmi_tlv_rssi_chain_parse()
looked the vdev up only on the pdev named in the event and returned
-EPROTO when it was not there. That drops the whole event, so
fw_stats_done is never completed and every sta_statistics call blocks
for the 1 s timeout.

Look the vdev up across the device with
ath12k_mac_get_arvif_by_vdev_id(), since vdev ids are allocated per ab
and a dual-MAC chip has two pdevs. If it is still unknown, for example
an MLO link vdev the host already tore down, skip that entry with a
debug message and still mark the event as an RSSI chain reply so the
waiter is completed. Do the same when the link station for the vif is
missing.

---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wmi.c
@@ -8745,10 +8745,21 @@
 		return -EPROTO;
 	}
 
-	arvif = ath12k_mac_get_arvif(ar, vdev_id);
+	/* Look across the whole device: vdev ids are allocated per ab, and on
+	 * a multi-pdev chip the vdev need not sit on the pdev in the event.
+	 * A vdev the host no longer tracks (an MLO link that was torn down)
+	 * is skipped rather than failing the whole event, which would leave
+	 * the requester waiting for fw_stats_done until it times out.
+	 */
+	arvif = NULL;
+	if (vdev_id >= 0 && vdev_id < 64)	/* allocated_vdev_map is a u64 */
+		arvif = ath12k_mac_get_arvif_by_vdev_id(ab, vdev_id);
 	if (!arvif) {
-		ath12k_warn(ab, "not found vif for vdev id %d\n", vdev_id);
-		return -EPROTO;
+		ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_WMI,
+			   "skipping rssi chain stats for unknown vdev id %d\n",
+			   vdev_id);
+		stats->stats_id = WMI_REQUEST_RSSI_PER_CHAIN_STAT;
+		return 0;
 	}
 
 	ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_WMI,
@@ -8758,10 +8769,12 @@
 	guard(spinlock_bh)(&ab->base_lock);
 	arsta = ath12k_link_sta_find_by_addr(ab, arvif->bssid);
 	if (!arsta) {
-		ath12k_warn(ab,
-			    "not found link sta with bssid %pM for rssi chain\n",
-			    arvif->bssid);
-		return -EPROTO;
+		/* Same as above: skip the entry, keep the event. */
+		ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_WMI,
+			   "skipping rssi chain stats, no link sta with bssid %pM\n",
+			   arvif->bssid);
+		stats->stats_id = WMI_REQUEST_RSSI_PER_CHAIN_STAT;
+		return 0;
 	}
 
 	BUILD_BUG_ON(ARRAY_SIZE(arsta->chain_signal) >
